{
  "id": "ospf",
  "label": "OSPF",
  "rfc": [
    "2328"
  ],
  "notes": "OSPFv2 common header (24 bytes) over IPv4 transport (protocol 89). Router ID and Area ID are dotted-quad identifiers, not packet addresses, so they are modelled as number fields \u2014 host primitives cannot reach them. The 8-byte Authentication field is not modelled: it exceeds the 4-byte BPF load window, and under cryptographic authentication (RFC 2328 Appendix D) its content is derived. OSPFv3 (RFC 5340, runs on IPv6) has a different header and is out of scope.",
